--- Negative sibling changes only its named channel; other channel remains contained. Expected N.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-FINGERPRINT-CONTAINMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient) openReq(v1, tPatient) lowerReq(first, v1, n1, pA, openedDependencies) lowerReq(second, v1, n1, pB, openedDependencies)
  =>* fpDiff REST:Cfg .

--- Opened fingerprint sibling actually changes fingerprints across transient inputs. Expected S.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-FINGERPRINT-CONTAINMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient) openReq(v1, tPatient) lowerReq(first, v1, n1, pA, openedFingerprint) lowerReq(second, v1, n1, pB, openedFingerprint)
  =>* fpDiff REST:Cfg .

--- Opened dependency sibling actually changes dependency hashes across transient inputs. Expected S.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-FINGERPRINT-CONTAINMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient) openReq(v1, tPatient) lowerReq(first, v1, n1, pA, openedDependencies) lowerReq(second, v1, n1, pB, openedDependencies)
  =>* depDiff REST:Cfg .

--- Safe observer nonvacuity: responses are reachable on both channels
--- with both candidates offered. Expected S.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-FINGERPRINT-CONTAINMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) lowerReq(first, v1, n1, pA, identityOnly)
  guessReq(first, pA) guessReq(first, pB)
  =>* answer(first, fingerprint, false) answer(first, dependency, false) REST:Cfg .

--- Candidate pB also records and permits the same public observer responses;
--- neither candidate is singled out by the identity-only commitments. Expected S.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-FINGERPRINT-CONTAINMENT :
  custody(h1) sealedVal(v1, secret, tPatient, h1) grantUnwrap(h1, tPatient)
  openReq(v1, tPatient) lowerReq(first, v1, n1, pB, identityOnly)
  guessReq(first, pA) guessReq(first, pB)
  =>* answer(first, fingerprint, false) answer(first, dependency, false) REST:Cfg .
--- Complete finite context census: all 2 envelope identities x 2 labels x
--- 2 types x 2 consumer nodes. Each case has a reachable pair, followed by
--- independent absence checks for EACH observation. pA/pB exhaust Payload.

